      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just want to highlight again that with this change we fully ignoring entry_timeout we received from the userspace in case we have a backing_fd.\n\nFor example:\nUserspace answered to the initial lookup with backing_fd, but with entry_timout equals to hour\n\nI that case I may assume that userspace is expected to receive lookup again after 1 hour probably to change their mind about backing_fd or introduce bpf.\nSo, basically with that change decision about lookup with backing_fd is becoming almost not reversible for userspace which is wrong to my opinion.\n\nWhat do you think about having something like that?\n\n1. Firstly check fuse entry_timeout and if it expired, fully relookup the inode to the userspace\n2. But fix the original problem by executing backing revalidate even if fuse entry_timeout hasn\u0027t been expired",
      "revId": "3492cc5f1642fa809c1a98fa9f3d45c90bd0be91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
