      "writtenOn": "2022-07-15T20:37:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This does the lower revaldiate if the entry we\u0027re revalidating has a backing path. If it was set up by the normal userspace lookup path, it will have a functioning timeout, and will go through the rest of the revalidate path as well if the lower dentry is still valid. If the backing path\u0027s dentry is not valid, or we get an error, we pass that along. We have to do that in case the backing filesystem returned something like ECHILD in particular, because that signals that we need to call back in a non-RCU context.\n\nThe block after this one checks if the parent entry also has a backing. Under that condition we currently skip the timeout checks because our backing lookup path does not honor the timeout we set there. We can fix that in a separate patch.\n\n\nChanging the backing on a timer doesn\u0027t make much sense to me, unless the timer is 0. If we want to go that route, it may make more sense to have a FUSE_REVALIDATE if only for bpf, so that we can choose to invalidate via the revalidate postfilter. We\u0027d either be able to use the future per-inode data to determine if we\u0027d like to change something.",
      "parentUuid": "78ab050c_79ecc480",
      "revId": "3492cc5f1642fa809c1a98fa9f3d45c90bd0be91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
